\name{randMBC-package}
\alias{randMBC-package}
\alias{randMBC}
\title{randMBC: Randomized Multivariate Bias Correction Backend}
\description{Experimental thesis package for randomized low-rank covariance transport in multivariate bias correction. The package provides: a simulated floating-point rounding helper and precision model abstraction (\code{fl_round}, \code{precision_model}, \code{unit_roundoff}); randomized covariance approximation (\code{rand_cov_approx}, \code{rand_cov_approx_pm}); a regularized covariance transport map (\code{cov_transport}); synthetic covariance operator generators (\code{generate_cov_operator}, \code{generate_climate_cov}); forward-error bounds and balancing diagnostics (\code{sketch_forward_bound}, \code{is_fp_hidden}); and a top-level prototype for dependence correction after marginal adjustment (\code{fit_rand_mbc}).}
\details{The package is intentionally narrow at this stage. It focuses on the numerical backend needed for thesis experiments rather than a full climate-facing user interface. The precision model (\code{precision_model}) encapsulates stage-specific rounding so that experiment code does not need to track format strings manually. The problem ensemble module (\code{generate_cov_operator}, \code{generate_climate_cov}) provides synthetic operators with controllable spectra for reproducible experiments.}
